The Mercedes-Benz C-Class 'AMG Sport Plus' was a trim level available on the facelifted W204 generation (roughly 2012-2014). It built upon the AMG Sport trim with additional cosmetic and feature upgrades. This evaluation is based on a representative model like the C250 CDI or C250 petrol with this package, compared to the current automotive market.

*   **price\_usd**: As a used car from the early 2010s, the price is significantly lower than a new car today. Prices vary, but are well below the $35,000 average for a new car. Score: 0.80.
*   **total\_cost\_estimate\_5yr\_usd**: While the purchase price is low, an older luxury car will have higher maintenance and potential repair costs than a new economy car. Score: -0.20.
*   **insurance\_usd\_yr**: Insurance groups for the W204 C-Class were moderate for its time (Source [26] mentions Group 34 for a C220 CDI AMG Sport Plus). Relative to modern cars, this is likely around average or slightly below. Score: 0.00.
*   **maint\_usd\_yr**: Maintenance costs for a Mercedes-Benz are generally higher than average (Source [13, 28]). Score: -0.50.
*   **repair\_risk\_score**: The W204 generation is generally considered reliable for a Mercedes of its era (Source [32, 33]). However, common issues like timing chain tensioners on some engines, steering rack failure, and suspension wear exist (Source [13, 28]). Risk is higher than a top-tier reliable brand but better than some other luxury makes. Score: -0.20.
*   **hp**: Varies by engine. C250 CDI had 204 hp (Source [7, 11, 14, 41]), C250 petrol had 204 hp (Source [7]). These figures are around the 200 hp average. Score: 0.00.
*   **torque**: Varies by engine. C250 CDI had 500 Nm (369 lb-ft) (Source [11, 14, 31, 39, 41]), C250 petrol had 310 Nm (229 lb-ft) (Source [7, 9]). The diesel torque is well above average, petrol is above average. Averaging these. Score: 0.50.
*   **cylinder\_count**: Typically 4-cylinder (Source [7, 9, 11, 14, 41]). This is common, so average. Score: 0.00.
*   **engine\_displacement**: Varies by engine (e.g., 2.1L diesel, 1.8L petrol) (Source [7, 9, 11, 14, 41]). Around the average. Score: 0.00.
*   **accel\_0\_60\_sec**: Varies by engine. C250 CDI around 6.7-7.1s (Source [7, 11, 31, 39]), C250 petrol around 6.8s (Source [7]). These are faster than the 7.5s average. Score: 0.30.
*   **top\_speed**: Varies by engine, around 149 mph (Source [11, 31, 39]). Around the 150 mph average. Score: 0.00.
*   **drive\_type**: Primarily RWD, some AWD (4Matic) available (Source [4, 7, 11]). RWD scores +1.00 according to the guide. Score: 1.00.
*   **transmission\_type**: Typically 7-speed automatic (7G-TRONIC PLUS) (Source [7, 11, 44]). A modern automatic for its time. Score: 1.00.
*   **offroad\_ability**: Sedan/Coupe/Estate body style, low ground clearance (around 11.2-15 cm or 4.4-5.9 inches) (Source [6, 9, 17, 20]), not designed for off-road. Score: 1.00 (based on guide examples).
*   **braking\_dist\_ft**: AMG Sport Plus included drilled brake discs (Source [18, 26]). Expected to be good for its class and era. Score: 0.00.
*   **size**: Length around 4.58-4.59m (180-181 inches) (Source [1, 6, 7, 9, 11, 17, 20]). Around the 4.6m average. Score: 0.00.
*   **wheelbase**: 2760 mm (108.7 inches) (Source [1, 6, 7, 9, 11, 17, 20]). Around the 2700mm average. Score: 0.00.
*   **body\_style**: Available as Sedan, Coupe, or Estate (Source [1, 2, 11, 17, 31, 35]). Score: 0.00.
*   **seats**: 5 seats for Sedan/Estate, 4 seats for Coupe (Source [20]). Score: 0.00.
*   **cargo\_space**: Sedan boot space around 475 liters (16.77 cu ft) (Source [2, 6, 7, 18, 20]). Coupe around 450 liters (15.89 cu ft) (Source [11, 17]). Estate is larger (485 liters) (Source [2, 27, 35]). Around the 15 cu ft average. Score: 0.00.
*   **rear\_space**: Legroom is generous for its time, but headroom can be tight for taller passengers (Source [2]). Score: 0.00.
*   **ground\_clearance\_in**: Around 11.2-15 cm (4.4-5.9 inches) (Source [6, 9, 17, 20]). AMG Sport Plus likely has a lower sport suspension. Score: -0.20.
*   **turn\_radius\_ft**: Around 10.84m (35.56 ft) (Source [4, 7, 11, 15]). Around the 36 ft average. Score: 0.00.
*   **mpg**: Varies significantly by engine. Diesels could achieve good MPG for their time (e.g., C250 CDI >40 mpg) (Source [11, 14, 39]), while petrols were lower (C250 petrol around 34 mpg) (Source [7]). Averaging these, it's around or above the 30 mpg mark. Score: 0.20.
*   **co2\_g\_km**: Varies by engine. Diesels could be relatively low for their time (e.g., C250 CDI around 130 g/km) (Source [11, 31, 39]), petrols higher (C250 petrol around 153 g/km) (Source [7]). Averaging these, it's below the 175 g/km average. Score: 0.40.
*   **electric\_range\_mi**: Not electric. Score: -1.00.
*   **charge\_speed\_kw**: Not applicable. Score: -1.00.
*   **style\_sleek\_vs\_boxy**: W204 design is a classic sedan shape, neither particularly sleek nor boxy. Score: 0.00.
*   **style\_aggression\_rating**: AMG Sport Plus adds aggressive AMG bumpers, side skirts, and spoiler (Source [2, 18, 26, 40]). Score: 0.50.
*   **style\_modernity\_rating**: Design is from the early 2010s. Looks dated compared to current designs. Score: -0.50.
*   **handling\_rating**: Generally competent handling, especially with the sport suspension (Source [2, 16, 35]), but not as sharp as rivals like the BMW 3 Series (Source [2]). Score: 0.00.
*   **ride\_comfort\_rating**: Sport suspension makes the ride firmer than standard models (Source [2, 33]), but generally acceptable for the segment. Score: 0.00.
*   **cabin\_noise\_rating**: Good for its era, but not as quiet as modern luxury cars. Score: 0.00.
*   **shift\_smooth\_rating**: 7G-TRONIC PLUS is generally smooth (Source [44]). Score: 0.50.
*   **steering\_feel\_rating**: Reviews often noted a lack of steering feel (Source [2]). Score: -0.50.
*   **adas\_score**: Offered some early ADAS like Attention Assist and Pre-Safe (Source [26, 27]). Lacks the comprehensive suites of modern cars (Source [24, 29]). Score: -0.80.
*   **visibility\_rating**: Standard sedan visibility. Score: 0.00.
*   **headlight\_rating**: AMG Sport Plus included Bi-xenon headlights with Intelligent Light System and Adaptive High Beam Assist (Source [2, 19]). Good for its time, but not modern adaptive LEDs. Score: 0.20.
*   **security\_rating**: Standard for a luxury car of its time, with alarm and immobiliser (Source [26]). Score: 0.00.
*   **screen\_in**: Facelifted W204 had an integrated screen, typically around 7 inches with COMAND Online (Source [3, 44]). Small by modern standards. Score: -0.80.
*   **infotainment\_ux\_rating**: COMAND Online was advanced for its time (Source [3, 44]), but the interface is dated compared to modern systems. Score: -0.50.
*   **smartphone\_connect\_rating**: Bluetooth connectivity available (Source [3]). No modern smartphone integration like CarPlay/Android Auto (though aftermarket units exist) (Source [10, 21, 22, 34, 37]). Score: -1.00.
*   **audio\_rating**: Optional Harman/Kardon system available (Source [10]). Standard system is likely average. Score: 0.00.
*   **usb\_ports**: Likely one or two ports. Score: -0.50.
*   **comfort\_feature\_score**: Heated front seats, dual-zone climate control, power seats available (Source [26, 40]). Good level of comfort features for its era. Score: 0.20.
*   **convenience\_feature\_score**: Parking sensors, rearview camera available (Source [18, 26, 38]). Lacks modern convenience tech like 360 cameras, advanced parking aids. Score: -0.20.
*   **brand\_prestige\_rating**: Mercedes-Benz is a high-prestige brand. Score: 0.80.
*   **model\_prestige\_rating**: C-Class is a core, mid-range model for Mercedes-Benz. Score: 0.00.
*   **trim\_prestige\_rating**: AMG Sport Plus was a desirable, higher-end trim package, but not a full AMG performance model. Score: 0.00.
*   **interior\_luxury\_rating**: AMG Sport Plus added Artico/Dinamica upholstery with red stitching, AMG sports seats, and other accents (Source [2, 19, 26, 40]). Quality was good for its era (Source [2, 16]), but materials and design are dated compared to modern luxury interiors. Score: 0.30.
*   **interior\_tech\_focus\_rating**: Featured an integrated screen and COMAND Online, but overall tech integration is minimal compared to modern screen-focused interiors. Score: -0.70.

